  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 103.64 Treatment technique requirement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 103.64 “Treatment technique requirement” means a requirement of Env-Dw 716 or Env-Dw 717 which specifies for a contaminant a specific treatment technique(s) known to the department which leads to a reduction in the level of such contaminant sufficient to comply with the requirements of subtitle Env-Dw and Env-Ws 300 until such rules are moved to subtitle Env-Dw.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 100) #10606, eff 6-1-14; renumbered by #10770 (from Env-Dw 103.62); renumbered by #12180 (from Env-Dw 103.63)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw100.html"
